# Trivy vulnerability ignores.
#
# Format: one CVE id per line (comments with '#'). Keep every entry
# justified and paired with a removal condition — mirror the template's
# pip-audit ignore convention (see commit "Ignore a vulnerability
# originating from pygments").

# node-tar Denial of Service via a crafted gzip bomb.
#
# We have to ignore this for now: tar is pulled in transitively by
# @anthropic-ai/claude-code, installed globally (`npm install -g`) in
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile, so there is no package.json / lockfile /
# overrides we control, and the current `@latest` still resolves
# tar 7.5.15 (< the fixed 7.5.19).
#
# Low real-world risk: it is a DoS (not RCE/priv-esc) in a build-time
# tool, inside a local dev sandbox behind a deny-by-default firewall —
# consistent with the gate's own policy of blocking only CRITICALs that
# actually matter for this image.
#
# TODO: Remove this when @anthropic-ai/claude-code ships tar >= 7.5.19.
# See:
# - https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59873
# - https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59873
